{"id":"aqft-eft-amplitudes","kind":"A","order":984,"items":[{"id":"def-aqft-eft-scattering-channel","kind":"definition","domain":"physics","title":"Gapped scalar EFT forward channel and matched coefficient data","reference":"items/def-aqft-eft-scattering-channel.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored draft; exact assigned contract; readiness recorded separately.","dependency_level":1,"deps":["def-aqft-scattering-amplitude-input","def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension"],"dependency_roles":{"def-aqft-scattering-amplitude-input":"formulation-prerequisite","def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension":"formulation-prerequisite"},"inventory_expansion_required":false,"statement":"Use natural units $c=\\hbar=1$ on four-dimensional Minkowski space $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$. Let $\\phi\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$ be a real, Grassmann-even (commuting) scalar field of engineering dimension one, with a stable one-particle state of pole mass $m>0$; here stable means an isolated real mass pole with zero decay width. Stability and the existence of this state are physical input data; no construction of a state is asserted. An effective field theory (EFT) here is the selected local low-energy representative organized in powers of its cutoff; its exact amplitude is separate supplied model data. For the finite-jet local-operator convention, use the complexification for the finite-jet algebra and impose the usual reality condition on $\\phi$. Take one field species, maximum jet order $r=1$, polynomial degree at most $q=4$, weight $D=8$, trivial internal group, and the standard Lorentz tensor action with contractions formed using $\\eta$. The real operator $\\mathcal O_8=(\\partial_\\mu\\phi\\,\\partial^\\mu\\phi)^2$ is then a local scalar of engineering dimension eight. Its coefficient in a chosen local representative is written\n\n$$\\mathcal L_{\\mathrm{EFT}}=-\\frac12\\partial_\\mu\\phi\\,\\partial^\\mu\\phi-\\frac12m^2\\phi^2+\\frac{C_8(\\mu_*)}{\\Lambda^4}\\mathcal O_8+\\cdots,$$\n\nwhere $\\Lambda>2m$ is the positive energy cutoff of the EFT description, $0<\\mu_*<\\Lambda$ is the chosen scale at which the coefficient and matching identity are specified, and $C_8(\\mu_*)\\in\\mathbb R$ is dimensionless in the fixed coefficient convention and local representative. No basis-independence under field redefinitions, equations of motion, or integration by parts is asserted for $C_8$ itself.\n\nThe amplitude data consist of an identical-scalar $2\\to2$ amplitude $\\mathcal A(s,t,u)$ and real on-shell momenta $p_j$ with $p_j^2=-m^2$, $p_1+p_2=p_3+p_4$, and\n\n$$s=-(p_1+p_2)^2,\\qquad t=-(p_1-p_3)^2,\\qquad u=-(p_1-p_4)^2,\\qquad s+t+u=4m^2.$$\n\nThe forward slice is $A(s)=\\mathcal A(s,0,4m^2-s)$ and assume $A(s)=A(4m^2-s)$ wherever both sides are defined. When the full $t$-dependent amplitude is supplied, use the partial-wave normalization\n\n$$\\mathcal A(s,t,u)=16\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{s}{s-4m^2}}\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{\\infty}(2\\ell+1)P_\\ell\\!\\left(1+\\frac{2t}{s-4m^2}\\right)a_\\ell(s),\\qquad P_\\ell(1)=1.$$\n\nHere $\\ell=0,1,2,\\ldots$, $P_\\ell$ is the Legendre polynomial, and $a_\\ell(s)$ is the partial-wave coefficient. The formula is a normalization convention when a full amplitude is supplied; it does not assert convergence or unitarity by itself.\n\nThe $S$-matrix convention is $S=1+i(2\\pi)^4\\delta^4(p_{\\mathrm{out}}-p_{\\mathrm{in}})\\mathcal A+\\cdots$. The channel adopts the forward optical-theorem input $\\operatorname{Im}A(s+i0)\\ge0$ for $s>4m^2$ in this normalization. This sign is an assumption on the supplied amplitude data, not a deduction from the EFT truncation.\n\nPut $\\nu_0=2m^2$ and $v=s-2m^2$, so $u-2m^2=-v$. Let the specified finite list contain every isolated variable simple pole in the subthreshold interval, with real locations $p_j\\in(0,4m^2)\\setminus\\{2m^2\\}$ and real residues $r_j$. For the dimensionless amplitude convention above, $r_j$ has mass dimension two. Define the crossing-symmetric pole subtraction\n\n$$P(s)=\\sum_j\\left(\\frac{r_j}{s-p_j}+\\frac{r_j}{4m^2-p_j-s}\\right),\\qquad B(v)=A(2m^2+v)-P(2m^2+v).$$\n\nThe exact amplitude data are required to be crossing even and real analytic, with $B(-v)=B(v)$, $B(\\overline v)=\\overline{B(v)}$, and $B$ holomorphic on\n\n$$\\Omega_{\\nu_0}=\\mathbb C\\setminus\\bigl(( -\\infty,-\\nu_0]\\cup[\\nu_0,\\infty)\\bigr).$$\n\nThere is no massless pole or cut at the forward point $t=0$. Require finite upper and lower cut-boundary values except at $\\pm\\nu_0$. Also require $B$ to extend continuously from each open half-plane onto every compact segment of either real cut bank avoiding $\\pm\\nu_0$. This is an extra admissibility assumption on the supplied data, not a consequence of finite pointwise boundary values or a claim about every quantum field theory. Require the uniform high-energy condition $B(w)=o(|w|^2)$ as $|w|\\to\\infty$ in the closed upper half-plane including upper cut-bank limits, and vanishing endpoint arcs for the cut integrals. For $\\nu>\\nu_0$, let $\\rho(\\nu)=\\operatorname{Im}B(\\nu+i0)$ and assign $\\rho(\\nu_0)=0$ by convention, without asserting a threshold boundary limit; changing this one endpoint value changes no Riemann integral; require $\\rho\\ge0$, local Riemann integrability on every compact subinterval of $[\\nu_0,\\infty)$, and finite convergence of $\\int_{\\nu_0}^{\\infty}\\rho(\\nu)\\nu^{-3}\\,d\\nu$. For every real $|v|<\\nu_0$, the upper- and lower-bank integrals of $[B(x)-B(0)]/[x^2(x-v)]$ are required to exist as finite improper Riemann limits. The positive gap $m>0$ and these analytic and spectral assumptions are IR and UV input conditions; they are not derived from a finite regulator.\n\nDefine the first nonconstant even forward coefficient by $c_1=B''(0)/2!$, of mass dimension $-4$. Exact matching at $\\mu_*$ is a supplied datum of the form\n\n$$c_1=\\frac{4C_8(\\mu_*)}{\\Lambda^4}+\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}},$$\n\nwhere $\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}}\\in\\mathbb R$ has mass dimension $-4$ and contains every other contribution to this exact $v^2$ coefficient, including other operators, loops, and matching or truncation effects. The identity is an assumption to be checked for a selected model, not a conclusion of this definition. Setting $\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}}=0$ is an additional exact retained-order matching condition; power counting alone does not set it to zero.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Allan Adams et al., Causality, Analyticity and an IR Obstruction to UV Completion","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0602178","locator":"Section 4, PDF pp. 14–20, forward analyticity, mass-gap regulation, poles, cuts, and the optical-theorem sign."},{"title":"Claudia de Rham et al., Positivity Bounds for Scalar Theories","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1702.06134","locator":"Full five-page paper; §§2.1–2.2, equations (1)–(15), PDF pp. 1–3."},{"title":"Ivano Basile et al., Lectures in Quantum Gravity","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.08690.pdf","locator":"Full 303-page lecture-notes PDF; §§3.2.1–3.3.1, printed pp. 90–98."},{"title":"C. P. Burgess, Introduction to Effective Field Theory","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053","locator":"Full 55-page review; §§2.2.1, 2.2.3–2.2.4, and the opening of §2.2.5, printed pp. 20–25."}]},"library":"physics","category":"advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry","physical_scope":"Conditional data interface for one massive identical-real-scalar forward channel and one fixed local EFT representative. It constructs no Hilbert space, S-matrix, continuum measure, or empirical result, and it gives no universal sign for off-shell operator coefficients.","justified_by":[],"proof_strategy":"direct"},{"id":"pthm-aqft-forward-positivity-wilson-coefficient","kind":"physics-theorem","domain":"physics","title":"Forward positivity for a matched scalar EFT coefficient","reference":"items/pthm-aqft-forward-positivity-wilson-coefficient.md","design_state":"Step 1 authored draft; exact assigned contract; readiness recorded separately.","dependency_level":4,"deps":["def-aqft-eft-scattering-channel","thm-aqft-gapped-scalar-forward-positivity","prop-aqft-quartic-contact-jet-matching"],"dependency_roles":{"def-aqft-eft-scattering-channel":"formulation-prerequisite","thm-aqft-gapped-scalar-forward-positivity":"mathematical-premise","prop-aqft-quartic-contact-jet-matching":"mathematical-premise"},"inventory_expansion_required":false,"statement":"Let $m>0$, $\\Lambda>2m$, and $0<\\mu_*<\\Lambda$. Use natural units and the four-dimensional Minkowski metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$. Let $\\phi$ be a real scalar of engineering dimension one with a stable one-particle pole of mass $m$, where stable means an isolated real mass pole with zero decay width. In the convention $S=1+i(2\\pi)^4\\delta^4(p_{\\mathrm{out}}-p_{\\mathrm{in}})\\mathcal A+\\cdots$, let $A(s)=\\mathcal A(s,0,4m^2-s)$ be the forward amplitude for identical on-shell external momenta $p_j^2=-m^2$, $p_1+p_2=p_3+p_4$, with $s=-(p_1+p_2)^2$, $t=-(p_1-p_3)^2$, $u=-(p_1-p_4)^2$, $s+t+u=4m^2$, and crossing $A(s)=A(4m^2-s)$. For a finite crossing-paired sum containing every stable variable simple pole in the open subthreshold interval\n\n$$P(s)=\\sum_j\\left(\\frac{r_j}{s-p_j}+\\frac{r_j}{4m^2-p_j-s}\\right),\\qquad r_j\\in\\mathbb R,\\quad p_j\\in(0,4m^2)\\setminus\\{2m^2\\},$$\n\nPut $\\nu_0=2m^2$, $v=s-2m^2$, and $B(v)=A(2m^2+v)-P(2m^2+v)$. Require $B(-v)=B(v)$, $B(\\overline v)=\\overline{B(v)}$, and holomorphy on $\\mathbb C\\setminus(( -\\infty,-\\nu_0]\\cup[\\nu_0,\\infty))$. Require finite upper and lower cut-boundary values except at $\\pm\\nu_0$, and require $B$ to extend continuously from each open half-plane onto every compact cut-bank segment avoiding $\\pm\\nu_0$. This compact-bank continuity is an explicit admissibility input. Also require vanishing endpoint arcs and $B(w)=o(|w|^2)$ uniformly as $|w|\\to\\infty$ in the closed upper half-plane including upper cut-bank limits. Let $\\rho(\\nu)=\\operatorname{Im}B(\\nu+i0)$ for $\\nu>\\nu_0$, extended by $\\rho(\\nu_0)=0$ without asserting a threshold boundary limit. Require $\\rho$ to be nonnegative and Riemann integrable on every compact subinterval of $[\\nu_0,\\infty)$, with finite $\\int_{\\nu_0}^{\\infty}\\rho(\\nu)\\nu^{-3}\\,d\\nu$. For every real $|v|<\\nu_0$, require the upper/lower boundary-bank integrals of $[B(x)-B(0)]/[x^2(x-v)]$ to exist as finite improper Riemann limits. Assume no massless pole or cut reaches $t=0$. Define $c_1=B''(0)/2!$.\n\nAt the fixed matching scale $\\mu_*$, suppose the selected local representative contains the real dimension-eight interaction $C_8(\\mu_*)(\\partial_\\mu\\phi\\,\\partial^\\mu\\phi)^2/\\Lambda^4$, with $C_8(\\mu_*)$ dimensionless, and the exact matched coefficient identity is $c_1=4C_8(\\mu_*)/\\Lambda^4+\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}}$, where $\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}}$ has mass dimension $-4$ and includes every other contribution to the exact $v^2$ coefficient. Then\n\n$$C_8(\\mu_*)+\\frac{\\Lambda^4}{4}\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}}\\ge0.$$\n\nIf the exact retained-order matching condition additionally gives $\\Delta_{\\mathrm{match}}=0$, then $C_8(\\mu_*)\\ge0$. The result is only a necessary bound on this specified matched channel combination; it asserts neither that a full amplitude exists for every coefficient passing the bound nor that every off-shell operator coefficient has a universal sign.","provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Allan Adams et al., Causality, Analyticity and an IR Obstruction to UV Completion","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0602178","locator":"Section 4, PDF pp. 14–20, forward contour, pole subtraction, mass gap, and optical-theorem positivity."},{"title":"Claudia de Rham et al., Positivity Bounds for Scalar Theories","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1702.06134","locator":"Full five-page paper; §§2.1–2.2,