The statistical suppliers are published definitions: they specify measurement models, IID assumptions when used, likelihoods, tests and confidence-set coverage, but they do not certify any particular collaboration’s fit. I’m adding precise local definitions for profile-likelihood ratios and calibrated p-values so the experiment records can name the methods without implying a universal likelihood or asymptotic law.
